    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]",
    "content" : "3. Results"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 42,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 317.52, 253.45, 550.804, 299.019 ],
    "font" : "CIDFont+F2",
    "font size" : 9.941,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]",
    "content" : "The results of single-cell simulations indicate that individual gaseous pollutants exhibit pro-arrhythmic effects in a concentration-dependent manner by altering the action potential."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 43,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 317.52, 207.281, 550.744, 253.059 ],
    "font" : "CIDFont+F2",
    "font size" : 9.941,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]",
    "content" : "Under healthy conditions, as the CO concentration increased, a reduction in the magnitude of the maximum peak of the ICaL current was observed and consequently, a reduction in APD90 of 23.6% (Figure 1A)."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 44,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 317.52, 126.761, 550.855, 206.979 ],
    "font" : "CIDFont+F2",
    "font size" : 9.941,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]",
    "content" : "As the SO2 concentration increased, APD90 was reduced up to 38.8%, also presenting a loss of the dome of the plateau phase (Figure 1B). The above is a consequence of the alterations in the ionic currents, which include a reduction in the magnitude of the maximum peak of the ICaL current, and an increase in the maximum peaks of the INa, Ito, and IK1 currents."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 45,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 317.52, 81.01, 550.813, 126.459 ],
    "font" : "CIDFont+F2",
    "font size" : 9.941,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0]",
    "content" : "Finally, as the NOx concentration increased, an increase in the magnitude of the maximum peak of the INa and ICaL currents was observed, an effect opposite to what was observed in the other two gases. This generated a more"
  }, {
